{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NXptwv5xKPN6MBWSsYFr4j","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Chapter 2: Cargo in Standard Crates\n2\t## *\"Why the shipping container beat the ship\"*\n3\t\n4\t**Exam domain: Kubernetes Fundamentals (44% of the exam) — competency: Containerization** [source: cncf-kcna-certification-page-2026-08-23] **| Estimated share of the exam: ~9% (authored allocation — CNCF publishes domain weights, not competency weights; see front matter) | Complexity: Mixed | Novelty: Moderate**\n5\t\n6\t---\n7\t\n8\t## Attention Budget\n9\t\n10\t**Total time: ~85 minutes | Recommended: single session if you're fresh; otherwise split at Taking Your Bearings #2**\n11\t\n12\t| Section | Time | Attention Cost | Best Time to Study |\n13\t|---|---|---|---|\n14\t| §1 What a Container Actually Is | 8 min | Low | Anytime |\n15\t| §2 What's Inside an Image | 10 min | Low | Anytime |\n16\t| §3 Registries, Tags, and Digests | 14 min | Medium | When alert |\n17\t| ☆ Taking Your Bearings #1 | 6 min | Medium | After a short break |\n18\t| §4 The Container Runtime Interface | 12 min | Medium | When alert |\n19\t| §5 The Open Container Initiative | 10 min | Medium | When alert |\n20\t| ☆ Taking Your Bearings #2 | 6 min | Medium | After a short break |\n21\t| §6 When Kubernetes Pulls, and When It Doesn't | 9 min | High | Peak attention |\n22\t| §7 Not All Isolation Is Equal: RuntimeClass | 6 min | Medium | When alert |\n23\t| ☆ Taking Your Bearings #3 | 6 min | Medium | After a short break |\n24\t| §8 The Crate, Not the Cargo | 4 min | Low | Anytime |\n25\t\n26\t**Attention Cost Key:**\n27\t- **Low:** Concrete, familiar concepts. Study anytime.\n28\t- **Medium:** New vocabulary requiring focus. Study when alert.\n29\t- **High:** Conditional rules that must be recalled precisely. Study at peak attention.\n30\t\n31\t*If you only have 15 minutes: read §3 and §4, then take Taking Your Bearings #1 and #2. Those two sections carry two of the chapter's three Fixed Points and the largest share of its exam surface.*\n32\t\n33\t---\n34\t\n35\t> *\"The crate outlives the ship. Standardize the crate.\"*\n36\t> — Lodestar Ledgers\n37\t\n38\t<!-- AUTHOR-REVIEW: outline § Open questions #9 preferred a real attributed quote (Malcolm McLean on containerization was the suggested well). No cached snapshot contains a verifiable McLean quotation, and Part 15 plus Ethical Guardrail #2 forbid shipping an attribution we cannot source. An original Lodestar epigraph is used instead. If the author can verify a McLean line against a primary source, substitute it here. -->\n39\t\n40\t---"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3a72b379-0c93-433b-90d0-591d2eea9a4e","uuid":"d124bbd7-bfdc-4cf3-a16d-0b64ae9ef1cb","timestamp":"2026-08-24T05:54:01.459Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\.pipeline-state\\ch-02\\draft-v1.md","content":"# Chapter 2: Cargo in Standard Crates\n## *\"Why the shipping container beat the ship\"*\n\n**Exam domain: Kubernetes Fundamentals (44% of the exam) — competency: Containerization** [source: cncf-kcna-certification-page-2026-08-23] **| Estimated share of the exam: ~9% (authored allocation — CNCF publishes domain weights, not competency weights; see front matter) | Complexity: Mixed | Novelty: Moderate**\n\n---\n\n## Attention Budget\n\n**Total time: ~85 minutes | Recommended: single session if you're fresh; otherwise split at Taking Your Bearings #2**\n\n| Section | Time | Attention Cost | Best Time to Study |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| §1 What a Container Actually Is | 8 min | Low | Anytime |\n| §2 What's Inside an Image | 10 min | Low | Anytime |\n| §3 Registries, Tags, and Digests | 14 min | Medium | When alert |\n| ☆ Taking Your Bearings #1 | 6 min | Medium | After a short break |\n| §4 The Container Runtime Interface | 12 min | Medium | When alert |\n| §5 The Open Container Initiative | 10 min | Medium | When alert |\n| ☆ Taking Your Bearings #2 | 6 min | Medium | After a short break |\n| §6 When Kubernetes Pulls, and When It Doesn't | 9 min | High | Peak attention |\n| §7 Not All Isolation Is Equal: RuntimeClass | 6 min | Medium | When alert |\n| ☆ Taking Your Bearings #3 | 6 min | Medium | After a short break |\n| §8 The Crate, Not the Cargo | 4 min | Low | Anytime |\n\n**Attention Cost Key:**\n- **Low:** Concrete, familiar concepts. Study anytime.\n- **Medium:** New vocabulary requiring focus. Study when alert.\n- **High:** Conditional rules that must be recalled precisely. Study at peak attention.\n\n*If you only have 15 minutes: read §3 and §4, then take Taking Your Bearings #1 and #2. Those two sections carry two of the chapter's three Fixed Points and the largest share of its exam surface.*\n\n---\n\n> *\"The crate outlives the ship. Standardize the crate.\"*\n> — Lodestar Ledgers\n\n<!-- AUTHOR-REVIEW: outline § Open questions #9 preferred a real attributed quote (Malcolm McLean on containerization was the suggested well). No cached snapshot contains a verifiable McLean quotation, and Part 15 plus Ethical Guardrail #2 forbid shipping an attribution we cannot source. An original Lodestar epigraph is used instead. If the author can verify a McLean line against a primary source, substitute it here. -->\n\n---","numLines":40,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1069}}}
